# Built on a copy of w5c/release (v4 at 145a70b plus the harness commits fc77fc1, d8ebc5d, d374759 and the fourth review's), outside
# any git tree; measured, never committed. FERO_SCRATCH_VARIANT names the REJECTED variants, kept only for their teeth (§10.10.8):
# timeout (a clock on the hold), forget (a two-tick memory of a held member's ask: the second review's blocker), counted (a stayer
# counts a held member), nojoint (the commit ignores the joint sets), nolead (a held member leads nothing: the second review's
# major), noviewcheck. The third review's three fixes are in the body (§10.10.6, §10.10.2): a HELLO carries the sender's holds (`v`)
